{"records":[{"id":"dz7jrpcd6g","title":"miR-20a regulates fatty acid metabolism in metabolic CRC","description":"Single-driver molecular events specific to the metabolic colorectal cancer (CRC) have not been clearly elucidated. Herein, we identified 12 functional miRNAs linked to activated metabolism by integrating multi-omics features in metabolic CRC. These miRNAs exhibited significantly enriched CRC driver miRNAs, significant impacts on CRC cell growth and significantly correlated metabolites.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-11-01T14:34:21.423Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/dz7jrpcd6g","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/dz7jrpcd6g"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kai","last_name":"Song","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Bioinformatics"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"8ddn9sdjys","title":"Molecular Classification for Phyllodes Tumors Improves Diagnosis and Guides Treatment Decisions","description":"This project aims to improve the understanding and management of phyllodes tumors of the breast, which are aggressive and recurrent fibroepithelial neoplasms distinct from breast cancer. Currently, surgical intervention is the primary treatment due to the lack of effective medical therapies, and histopathological diagnosis fails to accurately predict tumor behavior and clinical outcomes. To address this, we established a large cohort of phyllodes tumors and utilized multi-omics data to identify molecular subtypes, aiming to develop precise classifications for prognosis and targeted treatment strategies. Additionally, we created a gene signature classifier and IHC-based markers to define subtypes and predict outcomes. This research seeks to pave the way for precision medicine in phyllodes tumor management, enabling personalized therapeutic approaches for patients.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-03-28T13:24:59.024Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/8ddn9sdjys","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/8ddn9sdjys"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"qiaoling","last_name":"liang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Picture Generation"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"7gwtb7mgrr","title":"Genomic and Transcriptomic Characterization of NKTCL","description":"Natural-killer/T-cell lymphoma (NKTCL) is an aggressive and heterogeneous entity of non-Hodgkin’s lymphoma, strongly associated with Epstein-Barr virus (EBV) infection. To identify molecular subtypes of NKTCL based on genomic structural alterations and EBV sequences, we performed multi-omics study on 128 biopsy samples of newly diagnosed NKTCL and defined three prominent subtypes.\n\n ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-04-02T03:32:10.22Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/7gwtb7mgrr","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/7gwtb7mgrr"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Weili","last_name":"Zhao","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Genome Sequencing"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"4prxr9n5t6","title":"Supplementary material for Multi-omics Identifies Microbial and miRNA Biomarkers from Rumen Fluid for Susceptibility of Subacute Ruminal Acidosis in Dairy Goats","description":"Multi-omics Identifies Microbial and miRNA Biomarkers from Rumen Fluid for Susceptibility of Subacute Ruminal Acidosis in Dairy Goats","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-05-13T15:20:27.209Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/4prxr9n5t6","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/4prxr9n5t6"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"guanghao","last_name":"Xu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Goat"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"x29rjbpk8r","title":"Raw Data for \"A chemical screen identifies PRMT5 as a therapeutic vulnerability for paclitaxel-resistant triple-negative breast cancer\"","description":"This file contains the following raw data for \"A chemical screen identifies PRMT5 as a therapeutic vulnerability for paclitaxel-resistant triple-negative breast cancer\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-06-24T09:06:29.878Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/x29rjbpk8r","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/x29rjbpk8r"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Juan","last_name":"Wei","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Sheyu","last_name":"Zhang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Biologicals"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ymsbzh6c7h","title":"Multi-omics integration identifies cell-state-specific repression by PBRM1-PIAS1 cooperation","description":"PBRM1 is frequently mutated in cancers of epithelial origin. How PBRM1 regulates normal epithelial homeostasis, prior to cancer initiation, remains unclear. Here, we show that PBRM1’s gene regulatory roles differ drastically between cell states, leveraging human skin epithelium (epidermis) as a research platform. In progenitors, PBRM1 predominantly functions to repress terminal differentiation to sustain progenitors’ regenerative potential; in the differentiation state, however, PBRM1 switches toward an activator. Between these two cell states, PBRM1 retains its genomic binding but associates with differential interacting proteins. Our targeted screen identified the E3 SUMO ligase PIAS1 as a key interactor. PIAS1 co-localizes with PBRM1 on chromatin to directly repress differentiation genes in progenitors, and PIAS1’s chromatin binding drastically diminishes in differentiation. Furthermore, SUMOylation contributes to PBRM1’s repressive function in progenitor maintenance. Thus, our findings highlight PBRM1’s cell-state-specific regulatory roles influenced by its protein interactome despite its stable chromatin binding.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-12-15T17:28:23.177Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ymsbzh6c7h","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ymsbzh6c7h"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Patric","last_name":"Ho","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Xiaomin","last_name":"Bao","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Mass Spectrometry","Fluorescence Microscopy","Cell Culture","Western Blot","High-Throughput Sequencing","Quantitative Reverse Transcription Polymerase Chain Reaction"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"n99ytk6bgg","title":"likunliu","description":"A causal gut microbiome-prostate cancer link revealed by multi-omics: mechanisms, biomarkers, and therapeutic metabolite discovery","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-02-10T09:01:13.283Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/n99ytk6bgg","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/n99ytk6bgg"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"likun","last_name":"liu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Linked Data"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"zyzt62gbrw","title":"Multi-omics and Machine Learning Analysis of Human Plasma to Identify Biomarkers in Patients with Post-COVID Condition","description":"this data was used to generate the results presented in the articles Sequential multi-omics analysis identifies clinical phenotypes and predictive biomarkers for long COVID in Cell Reports Medicine and Multi-omics and Machine Learning Analysis of Human Plasma to Identify Biomarkers in Patients with Post-COVID Condition in STAR protocol. (https://doi.org/10.1016/j.xcrm.2023.101254)\nThese analyses aim to identify correlations between biomarkers and clinical variables, cluster patients based on their multi-omics profile, and find predictive biomarkers in patients infected by SARS-CoV-2, which is applicable to biomarker studies performed in various diseases.\n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-03-27T14:44:42.31Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/zyzt62gbrw","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/zyzt62gbrw"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mobin","last_name":"Khoramjoo","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Proteomics","Cytokines","Metabolomics"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ts5h8hxgy2","title":"Clinical and Histopathological Dataset of 170 Colorectal Cancer Patients from RSUD Abdoel Wahab Sjahranie, Indonesia (2020-2024)","description":"Overview\n\nThis dataset contains de-identified clinical records of 170 colorectal cancer (CRC) patients, including:\n•⁠  ⁠Demographic data (age, sex)\n•⁠  ⁠CEA biomarker levels (ng/ml)\n•⁠  ⁠Tumor histopathology (WHO subtypes)\n•⁠  ⁠TNM and Dukes staging\n•⁠  ⁠3D tumor measurements (length/width/height)\n\nKey Features\n•⁠  ⁠Population: Indonesian CRC patients from East Kalimantan (underrepresented in global databases)\n•⁠  ⁠Variables: 9 clinical + 5 histopathological parameters\n•⁠  ⁠Rare Subtypes: Medullary (85 cases), Signet-ring cell (11 cases)\n•⁠  ⁠Staging: Full TNM (33 subtypes) and Dukes classifications\n\nPotential Applications\n1.⁠ ⁠Biomarker validation for Southeast Asian populations\n2.⁠ ⁠Machine learning in cancer staging\n3.⁠ ⁠Epidemiological studies of CRC subtypes\n\nFiles Included\n1.⁠ ⁠⁠ clinical_records.csv ⁠ - Primary clinical data\n2.⁠ ⁠Data dictionary (PDF)\n3.⁠ ⁠Python scripts for analysis","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-30T17:57:35.984Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ts5h8hxgy2","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ts5h8hxgy2"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"chaesar","last_name":"chaesar","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/03sxt1c89","name":"Ministry of Education and Culture","grant_id":null}],"categories":["Biomarker","Histopathology","Colorectal Cancer","Southeast Asia","Cancer Staging"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"682mmrvgv2","title":"A study of Therapeutic and Prognostic Potential of GPCRs in Prostate Cancer From Multi-Omics Landscape, Shiqi Li et al.","description":"Original data for Figures in \"Therapeutic and Prognostic Potential of GPCRs in Prostate Cancer From Multi-Omics Landscape\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-07-04T19:22:44.599Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/682mmrvgv2","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/682mmrvgv2"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Shiqi","last_name":"Li","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Bioinformatics","Prostate Cancer","G Protein-Coupled Receptor","Omics"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":134524,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":151,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":134524,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":133931,"restricted":66,"embargoed":527},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2237},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":1387},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":627},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Centre","count":469},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":443},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":426},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":417},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":369},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":304},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn